## 2. Folder Structure & Next.js App Router

Next.js 16 uses file-system-based routing where folders define paths. A `page.tsx` file inside a folder makes that path publicly accessible. A `layout.tsx` file provides a shared wrapper for that route and its children.

```text
universe-connect/
├── src/
│   ├── app/                # Application routes, pages, and layouts
│   │   ├── api/            # Next.js Serverless API endpoints
│   │   └── ...             # Feature directories (dashboard, feed, etc.)
│   ├── components/         # Reusable React components (Modularized by feature)
│   ├── hooks/              # Custom React hooks containing shared logic
│   └── lib/                # Core utilities, DB clients, and AI wrappers
├── supabase/
│   ├── functions/          # Deno-based Edge Functions hosted on Supabase
│   └── migrations/         # PostgreSQL database schemas
└── public/                 # Static assets (images, fonts, icons)
```

