## 4. Deep Dive: Component Architecture (`src/components/`)

UniVerse organizes components by feature domain to prevent a massive, flat component directory. These exclude the generic UI components (like buttons, dialogs, inputs) found in `src/components/ui/` (likely generated by `shadcn/ui`).

### 4.1 Structural Layout (`layout/`)
- **`Sidebar.tsx` & `Header.tsx`**: The persistent navigation shells for the dashboard and internal pages.
- **`DashboardLayout.tsx`**: A specific layout wrapper for authenticated experiences.
- **`PageTransition.tsx`**: Wraps route changes in framer-motion animations (e.g., fade in/out).
- **`TopLoader.tsx`**: A progress bar displayed at the top of the screen during Next.js route transitions.
- **`PagePlaceholder.tsx`**: Skeleton loading states for pages while data is being fetched.

### 4.2 The Social Feed (`feed/`)
- **`PostCard.tsx`**: Displays a single post, handling media attachments, author info, and timestamps.
- **`SharePostBox.tsx`**: The input area at the top of the feed to create new text, image, or poll posts.
- **`CommentModal.tsx`**: A slide-out panel or dialog representing the thread of replies on a `PostCard`.
- **`PollCard.tsx`**: A specialized post type rendering interactive voting options and result progress bars.

### 4.3 Academic Suite (`academic/` & `academic/tools/`)
- **`ChatInterface.tsx` & `ChatPreview.tsx`**: The UI for interacting with Google Gemini. Manages message history state, loading indicators (typing animations), and markdown rendering of AI responses.
- **`ResourceGrid.tsx`**: Displays uploaded PDFs, syllabus files, and past exams in a responsive grid.
- **`StudyCircles.tsx`**: UI for finding and joining localized study groups.
- **`AddCourseDialog.tsx`**: Modal for users to select their current semester classes.
- **`FocusTimer.tsx`**: A Pomodoro technique timer built into the browser.
- **`FlashcardGenerator.tsx`**: Interface where a user pastes notes, and the UI polls the `generate-flashcards` Edge Function to produce interactive flip-cards.
- **`GPACalculator.tsx`**: A client-side utility to simulate "what-if" grading scenarios.
- **`SmartNotesEditor.tsx`**: A rich-text editor (likely using TipTap or Slate) with inline AI assistance capabilities.

### 4.4 Career Ecosystem (`career/` and subfolders)
- **`ResumeUploader.tsx`**: Handles Drag-and-Drop file uploads to Supabase Storage, then triggers the AI analysis pipeline.
- **`AnalysisDashboard.tsx`**: Visualizes the AI's feedback on the resume (e.g., radar charts for skills, ATS match percentage).
- **`MockInterviewer.tsx` & `MockInterviewerAI.tsx`**: Uses WebRTC or standard audio/video APIs to simulate an interview environment, sending transcripts to Gemini for real-time feedback.
- **`JobBoard.tsx`, `JobCard.tsx`, `JobFilters.tsx`**: Standard SaaS-like job discovery interface.
- **`SalaryInsights.tsx`**: Data visualization showing expected compensation based on major and location.
- **`AlumniDirectory.tsx`**: A list of graduated users who have opted-in to mentor current students.

### 4.5 Campus Life: Events, Clubs, Marketplace & Travel
- **`EventCreationModal.tsx`**: Form to create events, managing date picking, location linking, and image uploads.
- **`ClubGrid.tsx` & `ClubCard.tsx`**: Visual directory of organizations.
- **`ProductGrid.tsx`, `ProductCard.tsx`, `SellModal.tsx`**: E-commerce style components tailored for student-to-student transactions.
- **`RideFinder.tsx` & `RideCard.tsx`**: Displays available carpools, integrating with mapping libraries for origin/destination visualization.

### 4.6 Wellness, Messages, and Utilities
- **`TrendChart.tsx` & `MoodSelector.tsx`**: Recharts or Chart.js wrappers to plot a student's self-reported mental well-being over time.
- **`ChatWindow.tsx` & `ConversationList.tsx`**: The complex UI required for messaging. Must handle unread counts, typing indicators, and optimistic message updates.
- **`BusTracker.tsx` & `BusRouteMap.tsx`**: Integrates with external transit APIs or GTFS data to plot buses on a map.
- **`CampusMap.tsx`**: Interactive Mapbox or Google Maps implementation tailored to highlight university buildings.

