## 8. Deep Dive: Core Utilities & Libraries (`src/lib/`)

These files form the connective tissue across the application.

### 8.1 Supabase Clients
- **`supabase.ts`**: Uses `@supabase/ssr`'s `createBrowserClient`. It creates a singleton connection to Supabase initialized with the public anon key. It is safe to use in Client Components (`"use client"`).
- **`server-supabase.ts`**: Uses `createServerClient`. Next.js Server Components require specialized cookie handling (because they are essentially Node.js environments). This file securely reads and sets auth cookies to verify user identity before querying the database during server-side renders.

### 8.2 AI Wrapper
- **`ai.ts`**: Rather than copying `fetch()` calls all over the codebase, this abstracts the AI logic. 
  - `chat(history, message)`: Calls the `academic-ai` endpoint.
  - `generateFlashcards(text)`: Calls the flashcard endpoint.
  - **Mock Fallbacks**: If the API key is missing or the endpoint is down, this file provides hardcoded dummy responses so the UI doesn't break during development.

### 8.3 Tailwind Merge Utility
- **`utils.ts`**: Contains the ubiquitous `cn()` function.
  - Combines `clsx` (for writing conditional classes like `isActive && "bg-blue-500"`) and `tailwind-merge` (which intelligently resolves conflicts, so if you pass `p-4` and `p-2`, only `p-2` is applied). Every UI component relies on this for dynamic styling.

